Could you give me a complete rundown of one-time New York Giant, Andy Cohen?
— Joseph Smith, Brooklyn
Andy Cohen was a 5-8, 155-pound Baltimore nattve who grew up in Laredo, Texas and attended the University of Alabama. He played in Waco of the Texas League, then spent part
of the 1926 season with the Giants. Manager John McGraw fervently hoped that Cohen would be the standout Jewish player he was looking for in order to attract the large Jewish
population in the New York area.
Cohen, who played second and third base, had a three-year major-league career. He was originally brought up to play second base as a successor to the traded Rogers Hornsby.

